      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the textual claim as the speaker of the hateful statement",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the text_chunk 'what if i told you transgender is actually a mental illness called delusional psychosis' because the meme uses the first-person conditional 'what if i told you' to directly address the viewer, inviting them to imagine themselves as the one making the harmful claim. This creates a direct projection where the user is positioned as the potential source or believer of the statement, even though the text is presented as a hypothetical. The projection is onto the textual material, which acts as the primary vehicle for the user's imagined role.",
